{"author":{"id":"2462ded6f56967dde059994c39a506c79e39e5dfd10c5a07f07a23a5652a8353"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1776879246,"nonce":"sK1fvMMXyffpaBQsl0lBZRWEjXY=","title":"Set suspended:provider-overload status after retry exhaustion","message":"## Problem\n\nWhen `PROVIDER_OVERLOAD` retries are exhausted (72d63a1), the event flows through and triggers auto-resume loops until `max-resumes` is hit. Should set a distinct status instead.\n\n## Solution\n\n1. **SessionRunner**: When `PROVIDER_OVERLOAD` event is received (after adapter retries exhausted), set `suspended:provider-overload` status and stop — similar to `AUTH_FAILURE` handling\n2. **Auto-resume exclusion**: Skip auto-resume for `suspended:provider-overload` (add to exclusion list alongside `auth-failure`)\n3. **Watcher recovery**: Add `check_provider_outages()` to watcher that periodically retries `suspended:provider-overload` sessions (like `check_auth_failures()`)\n\n## Files to modify\n\n- `core/session.py`: Handle `PROVIDER_OVERLOAD` event type, set `suspended:provider-overload` status\n- `core/post_run.py`: Exclude `provider-overload` from auto-resume\n- `host/watcher/session_monitor.py`: Add `check_provider_outages()` with periodic retry (e.g., every 10 min)\n- `host/constants.py`: Add `PROVIDER_OUTAGE_RETRY_INTERVAL_S`\n\n## Tests\n\n- `test_provider_overload_sets_suspended_status` - PROVIDER_OVERLOAD event sets correct status\n- `test_provider_overload_skips_auto_resume` - no auto-resume for this status\n- `test_watcher_retries_provider_outage_sessions` - watcher periodic recovery\n\nREQ: REQ-032","files":null}]}